    id: "11fb595667268ce1e7bb",
    cat: "conflitti",
    title: "US hosts ‘productive’ trilateral talks to end Russia-Ukraine war",
    summary: "US envoy Steve Witkoff says renewed negotiations aim to ensure lasting peace before winter approaches.",
    preview: "US envoy Steve Witkoff says renewed negotiations aim to ensure lasting peace before winter approaches. United States, Ukrainian and European officials have met in Miami, Florida, to discuss a proposal for ending the Russia-Ukraine war, US envoy Steve Witkoff said in a statement posted to X. Witkoff said on Friday that “constructive discussions” tackled “potential avenues to de-escalate and conclude the war with Russia ahead of winter and advance efforts toward a durable and lasting peace”.",
    body: "US envoy Steve Witkoff says renewed negotiations aim to ensure lasting peace before winter approaches.\n\nUnited States, Ukrainian and European officials have met in Miami, Florida, to discuss a proposal for ending the Russia-Ukraine war, US envoy Steve Witkoff said in a statement posted to X.\n\nWitkoff said on Friday that “constructive discussions” tackled “potential avenues to de-escalate and conclude the war with Russia ahead of winter and advance efforts toward a durable and lasting peace”.\n\nRecommended Stories\n\nlist of 3 items\n\n- list 1 of 3Ukraine pushes Russia back in Donetsk as military, civilian casualties soar\n\n- list 2 of 3Trump announces Russian diesel deal amid soaring US fuel prices\n\n- list 3 of 3Putin tells Trump peace talks are unlikely, cites Ukraine drone attacks\n\nWitkoff said the meeting included “the E3, the European Commission, Ukraine and NATO”.\n\nThe discussions covered energy resilience, grain exports, security guarantees and “longer-term arrangements for Ukraine’s and Europe’s security to prevent future conflict”, Witkoff said.\n\nHe also noted the “productive” talks discussed “Ukraine’s post-war reconstruction and economic prosperity, including EU accession”.\n\nUS Secretary of State Marco Rubio said on Thursday the conflict had reached a dangerous “stalemate”, with the failure to reach a negotiated settlement raising the risk of further escalation.\n\n“The other way that stalemates end is through escalation,” Rubio told reporters, warning that the conflict could spread to neighbouring NATO countries.\n\nRenewed diplomacy\n\nEarlier on Friday, Russian President Vladimir Putin told US President Donald Trump that the resumption of talks with Ukraine is unlikely, citing drone attacks on Moscow during parliamentary elections last month.\n\nThe renewed diplomacy comes against a backdrop of deadly Russian attacks, including a strike on civilian buses in eastern Ukraine that killed 33 people. Authorities said the attack was the single deadliest attack this year.\n\nThe ongoing talks have been overshadowed by the US-Russia diesel deal on Friday. Trump blamed Ukrainian attacks on Russian refineries for surging diesel prices.\n\nThe deal was criticised by US lawmakers, Zelenskyy and European allies.\n\nZelenskyy called the agreement a “gift to Putin”. Hours after the deal, a Ukrainian drone hit a Russian fuel site.\n\nThe Miami meeting follows visits to Moscow and Kyiv last month by Witkoff and Jared Kushner, as Washington seeks to revive negotiations that have yielded little progress.",
    content_status: "full",
    source: "Al Jazeera",
    url: "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/10/us-hosts-productive-trilateral-talks-to-end-russia-ukraine-war?traffic_source=rss",
